---
title: Tartiflette
description: I hope you're not on a diet.
category: Mains
tags:
  - French
  - baked
servings: 6
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 60 minutes
created: 2026-05-18
updated: 2026-05-18
---

Preheat #oven{} to 180 C.

In a large pot, boil @potatoes{1%kg} for ~{20%minutes}.

Remove potatoes from heat, drain, and leave to cool.

Cut potatoes into small pieces and set aside.

In a #skillet{}, sauté @pancetta{250%g}(diced) until browned. Drain, and leave 1 Tbsp of fat in the skillet.

Add @onion{1}(thinly sliced) and cook in the leftover fat until golden brown, about ~{5%minutes}.

Add pancetta and @white wine{150%ml} to the pan and cook for another ~{5%minutes}.

Add potatoes and season with @coarse salt{} and @black pepper{}(freshly cracked).

Remove the potato mixture from heat and spoon half into an ovenproof dish.

Place half the @Reblochon{500%g}(sliced) on top of the potato mixture.

Spoon the remaining potato mixture on top of the cheese, then top with the remaining cheese.

Bake tartiflette until golden brown and bubbling, about ~{20%minutes}.

Serve hot.